# VT Challenge: AI Video Generation Web Application

**Feature**: `001-we-will-create` | **Updated**: September 17, 2025

## Project Overview

AI-powered video generation web application that transforms user text input into video content through multiple AI generation stages. Built with Next.js 15, Tailwind CSS 4, and integrated AI providers.

## Tech Stack

### Core Framework

- **Next.js 15** with App Router (NOT Pages Router)
- **TypeScript** in strict mode
- **Tailwind CSS 4.0+** with Shadcn/UI components
- **Motion** library (NOT Framer Motion) for animations
- **pnpm** as package manager (NO npm/yarn)

### AI Integration

- **Vercel AI SDK** for unified AI provider interface
- **OpenRouter** for text generation (titles, storyboards, prompts)
- **Fal AI** for image generation:
  - `fal-ai/flux-1/schnell` for initial generation (fast)
  - `fal-ai/nano-banana` for image editing (quality)

### Video & Media

- **Remotion** for video composition and playback
- **Next.js Image** optimization for generated content
- **16:9 aspect ratio** for all video content

### Storage & State

- **Local Storage** for project persistence (no authentication)
- **React Context** for runtime state management
- **next-themes** for light/dark mode

## Architecture Patterns

### Component Structure

```
src/
├── app/                    # Next.js 15 App Router pages
├── components/             # Reusable UI components
│   ├── ui/                # Shadcn/UI base components
│   ├── canvas/            # Canvas workspace components
│   ├── editor/            # Video editor components
│   └── generation/        # AI generation components
├── lib/                   # Utility functions and configs
├── hooks/                 # Custom React hooks
├── providers/             # Context providers
└── types/                 # TypeScript type definitions
```

### Data Flow

1. User input → OpenRouter (title/storyboard/prompts)
2. Generated prompts → Fal AI (image generation)
3. Images → Local Storage (persistence)
4. Images → Remotion (video composition)

